tion crossed 1104 units (budget 64) [chunk-114094], and baseline median degraded once capacity crossed 3570 units (budget 15) [chunk-114088]. Measurement series also show ceiling shifts after fixes (e.g., ceiling moved to 86 numa [chunk-114069], to 62 logit [chunk-114086], to 79 benchmark [chunk-114088]), reinforcing that capacity limits move with tool-work configuration changes. Recommendation: plan agent-host capacity around tool-work concurrency and contention headroom — shard shared pools proactively before contention reaches the observed ~2,900–4,900 concurrent-event range, provision so sustained tool throughput (on the order of 1,000–4,400 operations/sec) keeps individual resource utilization below roughly 50–70 percent, and tie budget-scaling triggers to the documented unit thresholds (~1,100–3,900 units) rather than to model-side metrics.",
